      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ is the set of all positive real numbers and zero.\n\n- $-\\pi$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $1.2=\\frac{6}{5}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $\\frac{6}{5}$. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $-3\\sqrt{7}$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{25}=-5$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $1.2$.",
