      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ is the set of all negative real numbers and zero.\n\n- $-4.5=-\\frac{9}{2}$: It is negative, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $-\\frac{9}{2}$. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $54$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $\\sqrt{16}=4$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $6.8=\\frac{34}{5}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $\\frac{34}{5}$. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $-4.5$.",
