      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{49}=-7$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $69$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\pi$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\frac{33}{8}$: It is negative, and it is a rational number but not an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $-\\sqrt{49}$; $-\\frac{33}{8}$.",
