      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$ is the set of all negative integers and zero.\n\n- $-8.5=-\\frac{17}{2}$: It is negative, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $-\\frac{17}{2}$. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{36}=-6$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $0$: Zero is included by the subscript $0$. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{9}=-3$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $-\\sqrt{36}$; $0$; $-\\sqrt{9}$.",
