      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ is the set of all positive real numbers and zero.\n\n- $\\sqrt{49}=7$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{34}$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $-7.2=-\\frac{36}{5}$: It is negative, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $-\\frac{36}{5}$. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{36}=-6$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $\\sqrt{49}$.",
