      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $-56$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $8.7=\\frac{87}{10}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $\\frac{87}{10}$. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $4$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\frac{11}{8}$: It is negative, and it is a rational number but not an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $-56$; $-\\frac{11}{8}$.",
