      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $\\sqrt{9}=3$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-6.3=-\\frac{63}{10}$: It is negative, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $-\\frac{63}{10}$. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\frac{32}{2}=-16$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $0$: Zero is not negative or positive, and this set does not include zero. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $-6.3$; $-\\frac{32}{2}$.",
